# DevNote Core

- Assume `Packages/com.devnote` version `2.19.7`. If this file conflicts with package code, trust the package.
- Bootstrap chain: `ContextStartup` -> `ProjectContext` from `Resources.Load("- ProjectContext -")` -> scene `SceneContext` classes. Finish every `RegisterContext()` with `Initialized = true`.
- Use one gameplay scene. Root groups in hierarchy: `= World`, `= UI`, `= Context`.
- Gameplay code depends on DevNote interfaces only: `IEnvironment`, `ISave`, `IAds`, `IPurchase`, `IAnalytics`, `IReview`, `ILeaderboards`, `IRemote`.
- `View`: only visuals, input, and sound. No direct SDK, platform, save, purchase, or reward logic.
- `Controller`: plain C# logic with constructor DI; may own `Viewer<T>`.
- In `SceneContext`, register controllers as `var controller = Register(new MyController(...));`.
- In `View`, cross-context references use `Holder<T>` and access only through `.Item`.
- `Viewer<T>` is the standard UI entry point. In `2.19.7` it lazy-loads the prefab; use `Show`, `ShowExpand`, `Hide`, `View`, `ViewExists`, `ViewIsShowing`, `OnShown`, `OnHidden`.
- `GameState` is a `MonoBehaviour, IGameState` handler. Reuse `IGameState.ParseState(data)` and `IGameState.GetStateDictionary()`, then add project keys around them. Use `TransferParse()` only for save migrations.
- `IRemote`: call `IRemote.SetDefaultHandler(key, ...)` before the first read. Bool defaults must be strings `"True"` / `"False"`.
- `IPurchase`: call `Purchase(...)`; reward and state changes belong only in `IPurchaseHandler.HandlePurchase`. Permanent products are declared in `PermanentProducts`.
- `IAds`: use `AdKey` + `AdShowStatus`; grant reward only on `Success`; interstitial flow must respect `NoAdsPurchased`, cooldown, and ad-block cases.
- `ISave`: prefer `SaveLocal`; use `FullSave` / `SaveCloud` on meaningful milestones, not every minor action.
- Sound uses `SoundUnit` + Addressables. Play via `soundUnit.Play()`, `await soundUnit.PlayAsync()`, or `Sound.Play(soundUnit)`, not string sound IDs.
- Project configs live in `Assets/- Project -/Resources` and are exposed through `Configs`.
- Naming: no abbreviations; private fields `_camelCase`; methods, types, and properties `PascalCase`; comments are rare and in English.
